{% extends 'wrapper.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Charter | {{ parent() }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
    <h2 class="text-center">Charter of MVforPalestine</h2>
    <p class="text-center"><em>Adopted by the membership on November 17, 2026</em></p>

    <h3>1. Name</h3>
    <p>
        The name of this organization is MVforPalestine, an unincorporated association. Its federal Employer
        Identification Number is issued in the name "MVFORPALESTINE." The name is also written "MV for
        Palestine"; "MV" refers to Martha's Vineyard, Massachusetts, where MVforPalestine is based.
    </p>

    <h3>2. Purpose</h3>
    <p>
        MVforPalestine is a political and educational group that supports the cause of Palestinian freedom. It
        organizes protests and presents educational and cultural events, and works to educate its members and the
        broader public about the history and current events of Palestine and Israel.
    </p>

    <h3>3. Membership</h3>
    <p>
        There are no membership dues. Any person who attends a meeting of MVforPalestine, or otherwise takes
        part or has taken part in its activities, and who agrees with its purpose, as set out in Section 2, and with its
        core principles, as set out in MVforPalestine’s
        <a href="{{ path('template', {template: 'principles'}) }}">Statement of Principles</a>, is deemed a member from that point
        forward. Membership carries no further obligation.
    </p>

    <h3>4. Meetings</h3>
    <p>
        <strong>4.1 General meetings.</strong> MVforPalestine holds meetings from time to time as called by the Steering
        Committee or by petition of any five members. A quorum for any meeting is five members, at least one of
        whom is a member of the Steering Committee. Decisions of the membership are made by a majority of the
        votes cast.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>4.2 Annual meeting.</strong> MVforPalestine holds an Annual Meeting each year for the purpose of electing the
        Steering Committee. The Annual Meeting shall be announced to the membership by email at least one month
        in advance.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>4.3 Remote attendance.</strong> Attendance and voting by Zoom or other comparable remote video platform is
        permitted at any meeting, including the Annual Meeting, and counts the same as in-person attendance for
        purposes of membership, quorum, and voting.
    </p>

    <h3>5. Steering Committee</h3>
    <p>
        <strong>5.1 Composition.</strong> MVforPalestine is governed by a Steering Committee (also referred to as the Executive
        Committee) of not fewer than three (3) nor more than five (5) members, elected by the membership. The
        number of members is determined by the membership at the Annual Meeting.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>5.2 Election and term.</strong> Steering Committee members are elected at the Annual Meeting by plurality vote:
        the candidates receiving the most votes, up to the number of seats to be filled, are elected. A tie for the last
        seat is resolved by a runoff vote between the tied candidates. If the number of candidates does not exceed the
        number of seats, the candidates may be elected by acclamation. Members serve a term of one year, renewable
        without limit. A Committee member continues to serve until a successor is elected, so that a delayed or
        missed Annual Meeting does not create a vacancy. A vacancy on the Committee may be filled by a vote of
        the remaining Committee members until the next Annual Meeting.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>5.3 Authority.</strong> The Steering Committee is empowered to make decisions on behalf of MVforPalestine,
        including but not limited to financial, operational, and administrative matters. It is the understanding and
        practice of MVforPalestine that the Committee will discuss significant decisions with the full membership
        where practical before acting, but the Committee's authority to act does not depend on obtaining prior
        membership approval.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>5.4 Officers and financial authority.</strong> The Steering Committee shall designate from among its members a
        Treasurer and one additional Committee member as authorized signers on MVforPalestine's bank and
        financial accounts. Each authorized signer may sign checks, authorize transactions, and otherwise act on
        MVforPalestine's behalf in financial matters.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>5.5 Treasurer's duties and financial transparency.</strong> The Treasurer shall keep complete and accurate records
        of MVforPalestine's finances, including all funds received and disbursed and all bank and financial account
        statements, and shall retain those records for at least seven years. The Treasurer shall present a full financial
        report at the Annual Meeting, and will make MVforPalestine's financial records available for inspection by
        any member upon reasonable request.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>5.6 Removal.</strong> A Steering Committee member may be removed by two-thirds of the votes cast at any
        meeting, provided the proposed removal was announced to the membership in advance. A vacancy created
        by removal may be filled as provided in Section 5.2.
    </p>

    <h3>6. Amendments</h3>
    <p>
        This charter may be amended by a majority of the votes cast at any meeting, provided the proposed
        amendment was announced to the membership in advance.
    </p>

    <h3>7. Dissolution</h3>
    <p>
        Should MVforPalestine dissolve, any remaining funds shall be distributed to one or more organizations with
        a similar purpose, as determined by a vote of the membership.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
